It is Saturday morning.
I stand in my apartment and look out the window.
There is frost on the street.
Everything is white and beautiful.
But it is also a very cold day.
I close the window quickly.
Still, I am a little cold.
It is a cold room.
I look down at my clothes.
Right now, I am wearing three sweaters!
They are all from Mexico.
They are some very thin sweaters.
They do not suit the Danish winter at all.
I look at myself in the mirror and laugh.
I look like a thick snowman, but I am still freezing.
I urgently need real winter clothes.
I must have a thick sweater and a warm jacket today.
I drink my warm coffee.
Then I take my bag.
It is time to go into town and shop.
